events.content:
Created `proxy.ts` at the project root. In Next.js 16, the old `middleware` convention is renamed to `proxy`, so the function must be exported as `proxy` (not `middleware`).

```ts
// proxy.ts
import type { NextRequest } from 'next/server'

export function proxy(request: NextRequest) {
  console.log(`[${new Date().toISOString()}] ${request.method} ${request.nextUrl.pathname}`)
}
```

This runs on every request (no `matcher` config = default). Add a `matcher` later if you want to skip `_next/static`, images, etc.

